{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-maximal-ideal-defect","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:maximal-ideal-defect","kind":"definition","title":"Maximal ideal at the unit coordinate","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-levi-form-defect"],"tags":["maximal-ideal","unit-coordinate","defect","singularity"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaximalIdealDefect","text":"maximal-ideal-defect.md","leanSource":"maximal-ideal-defect.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:maximal-ideal-defect\"></a><p>The <strong>maximal ideal</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}_1 \\subset A</code> corresponds to the coordinate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = 1</code> in the spectral fiber, defined as the kernel of the evaluation homomorphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{ev}_1 : A \\to k</code>. The point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = 1</code> is the fixed point of the antipode <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code>, marking the unique location where the Hopf and Frobenius structures interact maximally. The local ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_{\\mathfrak{m}_1}</code> captures the algebraic behavior near this singularity.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/maximal-ideal-defect.md","heading":"Definition","number":"8.13.2","page":"b/def-maximal-ideal-defect","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaximalIdealDefect","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/maximal-ideal-defect.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
